From ce87d29b39637c771db2249b274a06bf6a2b3e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: BCM4375 PCIe support, IPC rev 7 fixes,
 link-loss resume

BCM4375 (802.11ax combo chip of the Galaxy S10 family) on PCIe:

 - Chip and PCI device IDs (0x4475/0x4476/0x4477), TCM base as
   BCM4369/BCM4377, random seed footer (WCC_SEED); one firmware name
   (brcmfmac4375-pcie) for all revisions.
 - TCM ring indices honour PCIE_SHARED_2BYTE_INDICES. With a 4-byte
   stride only ring 0 of each direction was addressed correctly:
   control worked, data did not.
 - IPC rev >= 6: offsets 64..75 of the shared structure are
   host_scb_addr/size and no longer get the rev 5 ring update buffer;
   mailbox data (D3 inform/ack, deep sleep ack) goes as
   H2D/D2H_MAILBOX_DATA control ring messages when the firmware does
   not use the TCM mailbox; the H2D doorbell is rung once more after
   host-ready; the BCM4375 gets the bcmdhd common ring depths (rxpost
   512, rxcpl 512).
 - pcie_hostcap: -1 writes pciedev_shared_t.host_cap the way bcmdhd
   does (IPC version, HOSTRDY, DS_NO_OOB_DW, extended trap data with a
   host trap buffer, UR_FW_NO_TRAP), 0 (default) does not write it,
   any other value is written raw. The BCM4375 firmware only delivers
   tx/rx completions with it.
 - A D3 entry without acknowledgement no longer fails system suspend:
   the device is quiesced and re-probed on resume.
 - Resume: an intmask that reads all ones is a device that is not
   reachable (link down after a SoC sleep), not one that kept its
   state; it is re-probed. A wakeup source is held from the re-probe
   until the asynchronous firmware load has finished (at most 30 s)
   plus a 10 s grace period for the connection to come back.
 - pcie_warm_resume=1: a dongle that kept its power over a sleep in
   which the link went down is picked up again without a firmware
   download; the shared structure is checked for up to 200 ms after
   host-ready, and only if the firmware is gone the device is
   re-probed.
 - The cold-start firmware boot (download, ARM start, wait for the
   shared RAM marker) is retried with a chip reset between tries; a
   cold chip intermittently misses its first boot window.
 - msgbuf: the flowring is published before its hash entry and a
   packet for a ring that is not set up is dropped; a transmit racing
   with ring creation oopsed in skb_queue_tail().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
